<title>USA: TABLE - NUMAR Corp Q2 net profit vs loss.</title>
<headline>TABLE - NUMAR Corp Q2 net profit vs loss.</headline>
<dateline>MALVERN, Pa. 1997-07-25</dateline>
<text>
<p>(In thousands, except for share data)</p>
<p>		   for the three months  for the six months</p>
<p>					  ended		   ended</p>
<p>					 June 30,	   June 30,</p>
<p>				  1997	1996	1997	1996</p>
<p> Revenue		     $6,190    $4,106   $12,738    $7,079</p>
<p>Cost of sales and services</p>
<p>				  3,472     2,758     7,078     4,899</p>
<p>Depreciation of field assets</p>
<p>				  1,211	 933     2,269     1,845</p>
<p>     Gross profit	   1,507	 415     3,391	 335</p>
<p>General and administrative expenses</p>
<p>				    377	 412	 736	 790</p>
<p>Research and development expenses</p>
<p>				    616	 503     1,203	 973</p>
<p>Income (loss) from operations</p>
<p>				    514     (500)     1,452   (1,428)</p>
<p>Other income (expense):</p>
<p>   Interest income	     66	  84	 138	 158</p>
<p>   Interest expense	   (5)	 (8)	(11)	(15)</p>
<p>Income (loss) before income tax</p>
<p>				    575     (424)     1,579   (1,285)</p>
<p> Income tax expense	    23	  84	 104	  68</p>
<p>     Net income (loss)	552     (508)     1,475   (1,353)</p>
<p>Net income (loss) per share</p>
<p>				    .06     (.06)	 .17     (.16)</p>
<p>Weighted average common</p>
<p>shares outstanding  8,844,180 8,308,887 8,399,447 8,291,174</p>
<p>NOTE: The company said in the current second quarter, it entered into a merger agreement with Halliburton Co.</p>
<p>The company said it will become a wholly-owned subsidiary of Halliburton, and each common share of NUMAR will be converted into 0.9664 share of Halliburton common stock.</p>
